|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Burger Garden|Sub-chapter 10 - Burger Garden]]
|money drop = 1,250¢ - 4,937¢
}}

==Enemy==
Youcan is largely similar to the original, being a mid-ranged threat reliant on his powerful [[Wave Attack]]s and high damage to easily demolish your units while sporting two different traits and higher speed. His Area Attacks generate level 3 Waves and he carries an extremely durable [[Barrier]] (266,000 HP), making [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breakers]] nearly required to defeat him.

==Strategy==
When first encountered, Youcan's high damage means he can be lethal without sufficient [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]], so make sure you at least have them at 500% before tackling him in any stage. In later appearences where he is often buffed to 1200% or above, these Treasures must be maxed in all three [[Cats of the Cosmos]] chapters or else his stats are simply too much to handle. Despite Youcan's obscenely strong Barrier, the large amount of [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breakers]] and the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] make this a trivial issue, except on stages with harsh pushers for the former, like the [[M. Ost]]s in [[Wonders of Nature]]. There are even a few [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] and [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rares]] that are capable of breaking through with sheer attack power alone, to add on that. Include them in any formation and he'll be much easier to handle, as once Youcan's Barrier is destroyed he becomes vulnerable to crowd-controlling effects.

As with Two Can, the easiest way to deal with Youcan is to use [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] to block his waves (especially if the use of Barrier Breakers are considered, as Youcan's damage will demolish them easily unless he can't hit them), but options are generally limited due to his Area Attacks. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] won't be able to withstand him and his support for long, so Wave Shields that can outrange him tend to be more preferable. If Wave Shields are not avaliable, certain [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune units]] that can outrange him prove to be just as useful, and the same goes to rushers, if they inflict enough damage to knock him back.

Meatshields aren't generally useful against Youcan, since his high damage will melt through them quickly and allow him to hit much further than he should be. They should only be considered only when other pushers are in play, as their attacks can cause Youcan to miss.

[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] is a hard-counter to Youcan in most appearances, so use it if available.

